[recv] {"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"agentMessage","id":"msg_0b89129c34501917016a35ade8b554819382a5c1a0c5336606","text":"Implemented the schematic-only tscircuit project in [index.circuit.tsx](/workspace/index.circuit.tsx:1).\n\nWhat’s included:\n- USB-C PD sink input using STUSB4500-style custom chip symbol.\n- LM3409-style LED buck driver section.\n- 20 V PD-switched LED rail, sense resistor, buck inductor/catch diode, LED ring output.\n- Flicker-aware dimming path with PWM-to-analog low-pass input into `IADJ`.\n- `routingDisabled` board.\n- No tscircuit registry components imported; only built-in elements plus JLCPCB/LCSC supplier metadata.\n\nVerification run:\n- `npm run typecheck` passed.\n- `tsci check schematic-placement` passed with no placement issues.\n- `tsci build` completed successfully.\n- `tsci snapshot --update` created:\n  - [index.circuit-schematic.snap.svg](/workspace/__snapshots__/index.circuit-schematic.snap.svg)\n  - [index.circuit-pcb.snap.svg](/workspace/__snapshots__/index.circuit-pcb.snap.svg)\n\nBuild still reports non-fatal warnings about generic schematic-test footprints not matching some JLCPCB supplier footprints, plus missing `pinAttributes` on custom chips. I left those because this is explicitly a schematic agentrun test, not a production PCB/assembly pass.\n\n**TSCircuit Developer Feedback**\n- Confusing/surprising: docs showed `supplierPartNumbers={{ jlcpcb: \"C...\" }}`, but installed typings require arrays like `jlcpcb: [\"C...\"]`.\n- Most time wasted: schematic-placement cleanup oscillated on small net-label collisions around J2/C2/R2/R4.\n- Helpful improvements: clearer guidance for when to use full USB-C `standard=\"usb_c\"` versus a simplified connector symbol for schematic-only PD designs.\n- Friction points: `mosfet` docs mention `connections`, but this installed type version rejected it, requiring explicit `<trace>` entries. Some common-looking footprint strings like `led2835` and `inductor_smd_7x7mm` failed late at build time rather than typecheck.","phase":"final_answer","memoryCitation":null},"threadId":"019ee1a7-4edd-72f1-92cc-96f61f7553ee","turnId":"019ee1a7-4f00-7fb0-b77d-2cb6792163b8","completedAtMs":1781902833636}}
